<title>MEXICO: Mexico Dec silver output up, other metals detailed.</title>
<headline>Mexico Dec silver output up, other metals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest silver producer, saw output rise in December 1996 to 237,222 kg from 202,915 kg in December 1995, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said Friday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of metals and minerals production in the first four months follows:</p>
<p>    Product     Dec 96     Dec 95     Jan-Dec   Pct Chge Vs 95</p>
<p>    Gold	   2,293	1,862	24,115	  20.9</p>
<p>    Silver     237,222    202,915   2,535,726	   1.6</p>
<p>    Lead	  17,066     12,829     167,123	  -7.0</p>
<p>    Copper	30,600     26,290     328,093	  -3.3</p>
<p>    Zinc	  31,960     29,674     348,230	  -1.8</p>
<p>    Coal	 748,776    816,573   8,777,386	  19.5</p>
<p>    Iron	 563,195    557,259   5,667,539	  10.2</p>
<p>    Sulphur     77,366     76,272     851,920	   5.7</p>
<p>    Dolomite    80,451    115,816     926,933	   N/A</p>
<p>    Gypsum     296,648    269,855   3,696,315	   6.2</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 59,206     56,540     682,079	   N/A</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kilos, others in tonnes. Coal output in mineral volume. Figures revised from January-April figures given by INEGI.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530.))</p>
